From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 08:34:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fonts: Report the load state of @font-face rules in
 FontFace.status

A FontFace for an @font-face rule was created with the status "loading"
and kept it forever, and its `loaded` promise never settled, so awaiting
`FontFace.load()` on such a face hung. Keep the load state on the rule,
which the FontContext and the FontFace share, and settle the promise when
the state changes. A rejection is marked handled, because the object exists
whether or not the page asked for the font.

Fork note: first of four patches that stop Servo from downloading every
@font-face rule; this one also stands on its own. Meant for upstream; the
upstream-based version differs only in the promise API (RootedPromise and
TracedPromise there, Rc<Promise> here).

Relies on: `FontFaceRuleInfo` being shared between the FontContext and the
css-connected FontFace (upstream #45975/#46271), and on
`ScriptThread::handle_web_font_loaded` / `Document::maybe_fulfill_font_ready_promise`
as the places where a finished load reaches script.

Drop when upstream reports the load state of css-connected faces: on plain
upstream, `css/css-fonts/font-palette-add.html` then finishes instead of
timing out (it awaits `[...document.fonts][0].load()`), and a css-connected
face reports "loaded" once its font is in use.

Validation: `./mach test-wpt --release --processes 1 css/css-font-loading css/css-fonts html/canvas/element/text html/canvas/offscreen/text` (947 tests): font-palette-{add,modify,remove}-2 now pass and font-palette-{add,modify,remove} fail on the unimplemented `font-palette` instead of timing out (expectations updated); the only other unexpected result, font-variant-emoji-1 FAIL, also happens on plain ohos-main. font-variant-emoji-2 and matching/font-unicode-presented-as-emoji-outline already pass on ohos-main, so their stale FAIL expectations are removed here.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; written and tested by the agent, ported from upstream main to ohos-main's Rc<Promise> API)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
